  "body": "The `assert()` from `better-assert` isn't compatible with browserify and throws a TypeError when an assert fails.\r\n\r\n```\r\n    fs.readFileSync is not a function\r\n    TypeError: fs.readFileSync is not a function\r\n        at assert (eval at setup (/tmp/whatwg/streams/reference-implementation/run-web-platform-tests.js:40:14), <anonymous>:5163:16)\r\n        at SetUpWritableStreamDefaultController (eval at setup (/tmp/whatwg/streams/reference-implementation/run-web-platform-tests.js:40:14), <anonymous>:3692:3)\r\n        at SetUpWritableStreamDefaultControllerFromUnderlyingSink (eval at setup (/tmp/whatwg/streams/reference-implementation/run-web-platform-tests.js:40:14), <anonymous>:3721:3)\r\n        at new WritableStream (eval at setup (/tmp/whatwg/streams/reference-implementation/run-web-platform-tests.js:40:14), <anonymous>:2956:5)\r\n        at Test.promise_test (http://127.0.0.1:38453/streams/writable-streams/write.any.js:242:14)\r\n        at Test.step (http://127.0.0.1:38453/resources/testharness.js:1561:25)\r\n        at http://127.0.0.1:38453/resources/testharness.js:591:36\r\n        at new Promise (<anonymous>)\r\n        at http://127.0.0.1:38453/resources/testharness.js:590:20\r\n        at process._tickCallback (internal/process/next_tick.js:68:7)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis has a couple of unfortunate effects:\r\n1. Tests that expect a TypeError may pass when they should fail\r\n2. rethrowAssertionErrorRejection doesn't recognise the exception as an assertion and so doesn't rethrow it.",
